  {
    "sha": "9ca89a5ceb7c288b19f552ca44b182bc0ee566b5",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDljYTg5YTVjZWI3YzI4OGIxOWY1NTJjYTQ0YjE4MmJjMGVlNTY2YjU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "168627+NeoTech@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-27T20:53:39Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "168627+NeoTech@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-27T20:53:39Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(gate): the site tests run in the batch and release gates, and in quick when their inputs change\n\nThe site tests (python -m unittest discover -s site/tests, with zola and\nnode) ran only in the site job of release.yml, after the tag. They were\nred at three cuts in a row.\n\n- xtask/src/site_step.rs: a gate step that does not start cargo. It finds\n  python 3, zola (ZOLA or PATH) and node, runs the tests at the root under\n  the watchdog, and reads the unittest summary into the row note.\n- batch and release always have the step; quick has it when the diff\n  touches a path of site_step::INPUTS. A pin reads each path literal of\n  site/tests/*.py and fails when INPUTS does not cover it.\n- A missing tool is a SKIP row (never ok) in quick and batch, and a FAIL\n  row in release. A zola other than the pinned 0.23.6 adds a note.\n- unit_sweep::plain_dir: one expression on each OS, for the needless_bool\n  lint of Rust 1.100 (clippy -D warnings was red on Linux).\n- The gate skill names the step in each tier; decision in\n  docs/decisions/4133-site-tests-in-the-gate.md.\n\nFixes #4133\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
